   "id": "u4b",
   "title": "Gradual, parallel, DBR",
   "sub": "Seminar 7",
   "bites": [
    {
     "id": "p4-r2",
     "type": "read",
     "title": "The method",
     "html": "<p>Cycles = order / (P · S), rounded <b>up</b>.</p><ul><li><b>Gradual</b>: every operation, one after the other.</li><li><b>Parallel</b>: find the longest operation, add the head before it and the tail after it.</li><li><b>DBR</b>: drum (the longest) + tail.</li></ul><p>Then ask: does the setup need the previous operation's units?</p>"
    },
    {
     "id": "p4-f2",
     "type": "formulas",
     "title": "Formulas",
     "ids": [
      "s-cyc",
      "s-op",
      "s-grad",
      "s-par",
      "s-dbr"
     ],
     "html": ""
    },
    {
     "id": "p4-e1",
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Seminar: 20 units, parallel",
     "intro": "Op1 20 min (setup 20, 4 units per cycle) · Op2 20 (setup 20, 4 per cycle) · Op3 8 (2 per cycle) · Op4 15 (2 per cycle).",
     "steps": [
      {
       "html": "Cycles: 5, 5, 10, 10. Lengths: 120, 120, 80, 150."
      },
      {
       "html": "Longest: Op4 = 150. It is the last, so no tail."
      },
      {
       "html": "Head: Op3 one cycle (8), Op2 setup + one cycle (20 + 20), Op1 setup + one cycle (20 + 20)."
      },
      {
       "html": "Parallel = 150 + 8 + 40 + 40 = <b>238 min</b>. DBR = 150."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "p4-w3",
     "type": "read",
